      "writtenOn": "2024-07-22T21:32:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m more inclined to leave them out of the C++ API entirely because of the allocation. It\u0027s already technically a problem with the `DeviceDescriptor` since someone that sets the `deviceLostCallback` on a descriptor that\u0027s never used will likely leak the allocation.\n\nWe could maybe wrap the C++ structs and call the callback in the dtor or something with `InstanceDropped`? But it\u0027s not as intuitive? Forcing the user to pass a new callback on each function call feels a bit safer.",
      "parentUuid": "0963947b_2290daaa",
